		BookieBench


Can a model's probabilities be trusted? BookieBench asks a model for many linked probabilities about one
situation. It then checks four things:

coherence: whether a bookie can Dutch-book the answers, whether they are invariant to option and evidence
order, and whether updates follow a martingale;
calibration against sampled gold;
skill against exact posteriors, relative to the evidence-blind uniform_joint and to train-fitted priors;
evidence sensitivity.

